<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Isaac the Armenian</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 643</span> · Also known as Isaac (exarch)</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Isaac the Armenian was the Byzantine exarch of Ravenna from 625 to 643, governing imperial <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> on behalf of the emperor. An Armenian noble, he dealt with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombard</a> kingdom and with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a>, and in 640 his troops plundered the Lateran treasury in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a>. He died in office in 643 and was buried in the church of San Vitale in Ravenna, where his sarcophagus survives.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/isaac-the-armenian.jpg" alt="Isaac the Armenian" width="320" height="177" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sailko · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:San_vitale,_ravenna,_int.,_sarcofago_dell%27esarca_isacio,_m._643,_01.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
